---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, withBase } from '../config/site';
---

<Base title="Contact" description="How to reach the TextKit project." path="/contact/">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p>
      This is an example build of {SITE_NAME}. Public contact channels open when the site
      launches on its own domain — until then there is no monitored inbox for this address,
      and this page exists so the site structure is complete and honest rather than decorated
      with a fake contact form.
    </p>
    <p>
      When the site launches, this page will carry a real, monitored contact address for bug
      reports, tool suggestions and corrections. Found something wrong in a tool right now?
      The fastest check is to compare against the notes on that tool's own page — every tool
      documents its method, its edge cases and its limits in the open, for example the
      <a href={withBase('/tool/json-formatter/')}>JSON Formatter</a> page explains exactly
      how validation errors are reported.
    </p>
    <h2>Suggesting a tool</h2>
    <p>
      TextKit grows one sharp tool at a time. A good suggestion is a small, single-purpose
      text or data utility that can run entirely in a browser — if it needs a server, it
      belongs somewhere else. Suggestions will be collected through the contact address when
      it opens.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
